  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Coins for the orphans' wealth, a seal for the witnessing, scales for the fixed shares (worldly fairness). 6:24-28 (how much the poor guardian may take) is not glossed: a fiqh detail on which readings differ. 6: short-word flag at 15 (listen). STAGING v4: 6: at home, the guardian speaks with the grown orphan on 6:1 (testing him, both tafsirs), the young man answers on 6:8 (sound judgment), and the guardian hands him a purse on 6:11, coins plate; the prohibitions and the rich or poor guardian (6:14-28) are not acted. Witnesses (a small neutral pair: the verse gives no number) appear on 6:29; the purse is handed again on 6:30 and the guardian points to the witnesses on 6:33 (seal plate). 7: the heirs of a family (men and a woman, faceless) sit at home; one of them hands out a share on 7:2 (for the men) and again on 7:8 (for the women); coins plate, seal on the fixed share 7:18. No scales."
 },
